## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design consistent, beginner-friendly multi-interface APIs with shared auth and error models, reflecting real-world needs at large platforms.

## Key Concepts

- Unified versioning across REST, GraphQL, gRPC
- JWT-based authentication with common claims (aud, iss, tenant, roles)
- Consistent error payloads across interfaces
- Documentation and discovery considerations (OpenAPI support parity)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Unified error payloads
class ApiError extends Error { constructor(code, message, details){ super(message); this.code = code; this.details = details; } }

// Pseudo REST handler
function getProducts(req, res){ if(!req.user) return res.status(401).json({code:'UNAUTH', message:'Auth required'}); res.json({items: []}); }

// Pseudo GraphQL resolver
async function productsResolver(ctx){ if(!ctx.user) throw new ApiError('UNAUTH','Auth required',{}); return { id:'p1' }; }

// Pseudo gRPC handler
function GetProducts(call, callback){ const md = call.metadata; if(!md || !md.get('authorization')) return callback({ code: grpc.status.UNAUTHENTICATED, message: 'Auth required' }); callback(null, { products: [] }); }
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle token revocation and rotation across all three interfaces?
- What testing strategy ensures parity of behavior across REST, GraphQL, and gRPC?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical ability to design a multi-tenant auth bridge that handles both OIDC and SAML inputs, normalizes to a single internal JWT, supports a token-exchange path, and enforces per-tenant policy and replay protection.

## Key Concepts
- Token validation for OIDC and SAML
- Claim mapping to an internal JWT with tenant and scopes
- Token exchange semantics for downstream services
- TTL-based per-tenant replay protection
- Middleware enforcing audience, issuer, tenant, and scope

## Code Example
```javascript
// SAML-to-claims adapter (pseudo)
function mapSamlToClaims(saml) {
  return {
    sub: saml.nameID,
    tenant: saml.attributes?.tenant,
    scope: (saml.attributes?.scopes || '').split(' ')
  };
}
```

```javascript
// Minimal internal JWT issuer (pseudo)
function issueInternalJwt(claims) {
  return jwt.sign({ sub: claims.sub, tenant: claims.tenant, scope: claims.scope, aud: 'internal-service' }, privateKey, { algorithm: 'RS256', expiresIn: '15m' });
}
```

```javascript
// Replay protection middleware (pseudo)
function replayGuard(req, res, next) {
  const jti = req.token?.jti;
  const key = req.tenant + ':' + jti;
  if (replayCache.has(key)) return res.status(401).send('replayed');
  replayCache.set(key, true, ttlMs);
  next();
}
```

